 forward to help us  collect signatures in every different  way they're trying to pull back from  direct democracy because they fear what  the voters will do if the voters  actually are empowered to to reduce  union power at the local level we are  seeing a union attempts to subvert  direct democracy by attempting to  introduce fraud into the signature  gathering process and that's an ugly  word but there's no other way to get  around it the labor unions check out  these outrageous radio ads saying that  if you signed a ballot measure your  identity would be stolen and sold to  India I just got back from the  supermarket and those pesky signature  gatherers are back please tell me you  didn't sign their petitions I did is  there a problem  you put yourself at risk of identity  theft are you kidding me they even have  my signature I also read the names and  addresses on petitions were found in  countries as far away as India who knows  what they did with it I guess the lesson  is to be careful giving information to  anyone we don't know paid for by  Californians against identity theft and  ballot fraud supported by labor  organizations I laughed and laughed and  laughed when I first heard the air the  add air just like two minutes before I  was supposed to go on one night and it  was obvious to me what was going on I  can't tell you how many people when they  showed up at the stores would say that  the ad was what convinced them to sign  the petition they also hired paid  blockers these are big guys that they  would send out to the stores whenever  they would see a campaign worker  collecting signatures in front of a  store and there would be six seven eight  blockers deep with signs harassing both  the campaign workers as well as store  patrons who were interested in signing  the ballot measure wait so he was out of  cotton guess I walked him  it was shocking that they would go to  these lengths to disrupt which should  ordinarily be a respectful process but  again 